      "message": "Note: taking the address of a composite member (e.g. struct field) via a let-declared alias is not allowed. Something to keep in mind in codegen. For example:\n\n    struct Foo {\n        a: f32,\n    }\n    struct SSBO {\n        foos: array\u003cFoo\u003e,\n    }\n    @group(0) @binding(0) var\u003cstorage, read_write\u003e ssbo: SSBO;\n    \n    ...\n    \n    var foo \u003d ssbo.foos[0];\n    let tmp \u003d \u0026foo.a;  // --\u003e allowed\n    \n    ...\n    \n    let foo \u003d ssbo.foos[0];\n    let tmp \u003d \u0026foo.a;  // --\u003e not allowed",
